From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:59:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: OPLUS: list the USB
 connector temperature

The previous commit reads the connector temperature (USB property 10,
USB_TEMP, the downstream battery charger's numbering) for the SM8350
style firmware, but lists it only in sm8350_usb_props: the OnePlus Pad 4
binds the OPLUS variant, whose USB supply uses oplus_usb_props, so the
temperature did not show up there.

List POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TEMP for the OPLUS variant too. Its firmware is
the same Qualcomm battery manager with vendor additions on top, which
keeps the standard USB property numbering (USB_ADAP_TYPE, 7, is already
read from it); whether it fills USB_TEMP is to be checked on the device.
So that a firmware without it cannot hide the other properties from
user space, a failed temperature read reports -ENODATA, which the power
supply uevent skips, instead of the firmware's raw result or a timeout.

No DT change: the value comes over the existing pmic_glink channel.

Based-on: "power: supply: qcom_battmgr: Expose USB connector temperature" (Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>, lore 20261020-topic-usb_temp-v1-1-3dbe390f9834)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index d2baec2ee..7a0603525 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1701,6 +1701,13 @@ static int qcom_battmgr_usb_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 		ret = qcom_battmgr_bat_sc8280xp_update(battmgr, psp);
 	else
 		ret = qcom_battmgr_usb_sm8350_update(battmgr, psp);
+	/*
+	 * A firmware without the connector temperature answers with its own (raw) error or
+	 * not at all: report "no data", which the power supply uevent skips, so that the
+	 * other properties still reach user space.
+	 */
+	if (ret && psp == POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TEMP)
+		return -ENODATA;
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
@@ -1783,6 +1790,7 @@ static const enum power_supply_property oplus_usb_props[] = {
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_MAX,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_INPUT_CURRENT_LIMIT,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_USB_TYPE,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TEMP,
 };
 
 static const struct power_supply_desc sm8350_usb_psy_desc = {
